From 907ba542749c5b9f1c44175a59c549474b44d5a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Penev <alexander.p.penev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:01:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] compiler: one NodeKind, and a parameter schema that
 covers every kind

param_binding_table.hpp kept its own copy of NodeKind (`namespace pk`) so it
could stay free of the LLVM-coupled node.hpp, and `static_cast<int>(n.kind)`
bridged the two. The copy drifted: RotateX and RotateZ were added to NodeKind
at 11 and 12, which were TwistY and BendXY in the copy, so every kind from 11
upward was off by two.

A wrong kind does not throw - it returns the wrong SCHEMA, and a node whose
schema does not name its parameters simply has none of them bound. Measured
with an all-runtime policy, slots bound per kind, before -> after:

    Scale    0/3 -> 3/3      (schema said "s"; the node stores sx, sy, sz)
    RotateX  0/1 -> 1/1      (read as TwistY, schema "k")
    RotateZ  0/1 -> 1/1      (read as BendXY, schema "k")
    TwistY   0/1 -> 1/1      (read as TaperY, schema "t","h")
    BendXY   0/1 -> 1/1      (read as Scene, empty)
    TaperY   0/2 -> 2/2      (read as Plugin, empty)
    Tube     0/5 -> 5/5      (no schema at all)
    Cone     0/7 -> 7/7      (no schema at all)

Of twelve kinds only Sphere, Box, Translate and RotateY were correct. The
effect was silent: editing any other kind's parameter forced a full
recompile instead of a slot write, and classify_param answered Deform for
parameters those nodes do not have.

NodeKind moves to core/frep/node_kind.hpp, which has no LLVM dependency, and
both headers include it. The schema is completed for Scale, RotateX/Z,
TwistY, BendXY, TaperY and the six HEP kinds, and the switch is exhaustive
over the enum so a new kind is a compile error rather than a silent empty.

tests/test_param_schema.cpp asserts the schema names EXACTLY what each
constructor stored, per kind, plus the end-to-end slot count. A second copy
of a list that must stay in step with another is not decoupling, it is an
unchecked invariant.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B5ALyYbzrXTGtc7LqRPGCz
