From 9a35e01aebcad63b5763efd90c234b64cd90990e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Penev <alexander.p.penev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:49:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] core: parameters as an ordered vector, addressed by index

FD4's CPU evaluator was 90% hash table. Of the 45 ns a BoxNode::eval took,
40 were three lookups of short strings in an unordered_map; the arithmetic
was noise, and no amount of care with floating point moves a number that is
dominated by hashing "hx", "hy", "hz". A radius does not need to be FOUND -
its position is a property of the node's type.

params becomes a ParamStore: a vector of doubles in the node's constructor
order, with the names kept beside them. Each node addresses its own
parameters through an `enum : int` next to its constructor; name lookup
stays for the serialiser, the editor, the GLSL emitter and the binding
table, none of which is on a hot path, and is now a linear scan over at
most twelve short strings with no hashing and no allocation.

The order is the one node_param_schema() lists, and test_param_schema.cpp
now asserts the two agree by POSITION as well as by name - if they ever
diverge, a runtime slot write lands on the wrong parameter and the geometry
changes silently.

Measured, ns per eval, same 15 node types and 400 points:

    sphere  13.4 ->  4.4    trd     88.0 -> 14.2
    box     44.9 ->  7.3    poly   152.5 -> 35.1
    plane   52.9 ->  5.2    frame  339.8 -> 15.9
    tube   145.1 -> 50.7    union   55.8 -> 11.2
    cone    99.8 -> 18.6    rotx    60.7 -> 22.1
    shell  191.0 -> 103.6   trans   55.1 ->  6.5

Whole set: 100.6 -> 21.9 ns/eval, 4.6x. The float path stays BIT-IDENTICAL
to the original map-based tree across all 6000 samples - this is a change
of where a number is stored, not of what is computed.

Two incidental fixes fall out of the ordering: structural_hash walked an
unordered_map, whose iteration order the standard does not specify, so the
incremental cache key was resting on an implementation detail; and the
ConeNode constructor still took phi0/dphi as float.

